<title>BELGIUM: PetroFina has 13.33 pct of Italian well.</title>
<headline>PetroFina has 13.33 pct of Italian well.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian oil group PetroFina said on Friday it owned a 13.335 percent interest in a successful test well drilled in Italy by a consortium led by British oil exploration company LASMO Plc.</p>
<p>LASMO said on Thursday it had successfully completed the Gorgoglione well in the Tempa Rossa field in southern Italy.</p>
<p>&quot;A decision to develop the Tempa Rossa field is now expected before the end of 1997,&quot; John Hogan, LASMO's chief operating officer, said in a statement.</p>
<p>PetroFina said its interest in the whole Tempa Rossa field amounted to 20 percent.</p>
<p>PetroFina's interest is held through its 100 percent-owned subsidiary  Fina Italiana SpA.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
